-- title:
--   Central-norm twisted term in prime-degree cyclic base change
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields whose degree $\ell=[L:K]$ is prime, let $0<\alpha<\beta$ be reals, let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$ (a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$, continuous and extending the action on $L$), let $\sigma\neq 1$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$, let $c_0\in\mathbb{R}_{\ge0}$, and let $\varphi$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $f$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ be continuous with compact support. Two groups of hypotheses are imposed, summarised here: a central transfer hypothesis `hcent`, which states that for every $\delta_0\in GL_2(L)$, every unit $c$ of $L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K$ and every idele unit $u$ of $K$ such that the $\sigma^{-1}$-norm string $\prod_{i<\ell}\sigma^{-i}(\delta)$ of $\delta=\delta_0\cdot c\,\mathrm{Id}$ equals the scalar matrix of $u$ pushed into $GL_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$, and for any Haar measures $\tau$ on the centraliser of the scalar matrix of $u$ in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and $\tau'$ on the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t: t\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1}=\delta\}$ of $\delta$, and any finite non-zero $C$ such that, for all $0<a\le b$, every fundamental domain for the right action of the rational twisted centraliser meets the band $\|\det\|_L\in[a,b]$ in $\tau'$-measure $C\log(b/a)$ while every fundamental domain for the right action of the image of $GL_2(K)$ meets $\|\det\|_K\in[a,b]$ in $\tau$-measure $\ell\,C\log(b/a)$, any value $I'$ of the twisted orbital integral of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ (taken against the transport of the Haar measure of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ to $GL_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$ and $\tau'$) equals any value $I$ of the orbital integral of $f$ at the scalar matrix of $u$ against $c_0$ times the Haar measure of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and $\tau$; and a covolume normalisation `hC_H` for a finite non-zero $C_H$, namely that any fundamental domain for $GL_2(K)$ inside the band $\|\det\|_K\in[a,b]$ has Haar measure $C_H\log(b/a)$ for all $0<a\le b$. Finally let $\delta_0\in GL_2(L)$ and $b_0\in K^\times$ be such that the twisted norm class map attached to $\sigma^{-1}$ sends the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta_0$ to the conjugacy class of the scalar matrix of $b_0$ in $GL_2(K)$, let $\Psi\subseteq GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ be contained in the band $\|\det\|_L\in[\alpha,\beta]$ and be a fundamental domain, for the restriction of the adelic Haar measure to that band, for the image in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ of the rational $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_0$, and let $z$ be an idele unit of $L$. Then $$\int_{\Psi}\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(z\,x)\bigr)\,dx=\frac{c_0}{\ell}\,\bigl(C_H\log(\beta/\alpha)\bigr)\cdot f\bigl(b_0\,N_{L/K}(z)\cdot\mathrm{Id}\bigr),$$ where $\sigma^{-1}$ acts on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ through $D$, $z$ and $b_0\,N_{L/K}(z)$ enter as scalar matrices, $N_{L/K}$ is the idelic norm of the base change $\mathbb{A}_K\to\mathbb{A}_L$, the real constant being the real part of $C_H\cdot\log(\beta/\alpha)$ in $[0,\infty]$ scaled by $c_0/\ell$ and cast to $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the class-by-class analytic comparison, for a cyclic extension of prime degree, of a twisted term of the trace formula over $L$ attached to a $\sigma$-conjugacy class whose twisted norm is central with the corresponding central term over $K$, deduced from the central transfer hypothesis alone. It feeds the summation over all such classes in [`AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_centralNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_central_of_central_transfer`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_centralNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_central_of_central_transfer), where the enumeration of the classes and their multiplicities is handled separately.
